WEBVTT

00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:08.905
(screaming)

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.408
Were you killed?

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:13.910
Sadly, yes.

00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:15.453
But I lived!

00:00:15.536 --> 00:00:16.704
(both sigh in relief)

00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:18.331
-(dismissive sigh)
-ELLIE: Shh.

00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:23.628
Never had I felt so alive
than when I was so close to death.

00:00:23.711 --> 00:00:26.172
Just before Rudy
could suck me down his gullet,

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:28.758
I grabbed hold of that gross,
pink, fleshy thing

00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:30.426
that dangles at the back
of the throat.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:31.886
-Ew.
-Ew.

00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:35.097
BUCK: I hung onto that sucker,
and I swung back and forth,

00:00:35.181 --> 00:00:36.557
and back and forth,

00:00:36.641 --> 00:00:39.185
and back and forth,
and back and forth,

00:00:39.268 --> 00:00:40.937
-and back...
-(all gasp)

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.022
...and forth, and back and forth,

00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:44.899
until finally I let go.

00:00:44.982 --> 00:00:48.277
-And I shot right out of his mouth.
-(roaring)

00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:50.446
I may have lost an eye that day,

00:00:50.529 --> 00:00:53.032
but I got this.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:54.367
Rudy's tooth.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.118
Dang.

00:00:56.202 --> 00:00:59.497
It's like the old saying:
"An eye for a tooth, a nose for a chin,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.333
a butt for a..."

00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:03.668
Well, it's an old saying,

00:01:03.751 --> 00:01:05.544
but, uh, it's not a very good one.

00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:07.129
You are Super Weasel.

00:01:07.213 --> 00:01:08.673
Ultra Weasel!

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:10.091
Diesel Weasel!

00:01:10.174 --> 00:01:14.136
(gruff scatting)

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.054
(scoffs):
Huh...

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:16.889
What? He is.

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:18.766
Now, let me tell you
about the time I used

00:01:18.849 --> 00:01:21.185
a sharpened clamshell
to turn a T. Rex...

00:01:21.268 --> 00:01:22.770
into a "T. Rachel."

00:01:22.853 --> 00:01:23.771
-Yes, master.
-Yes, master.

00:01:23.854 --> 00:01:25.064
MANNY:
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:27.441
That's enough fairy tales
for one night.

00:01:27.525 --> 00:01:28.567
Come on, Ellie.

00:01:28.651 --> 00:01:30.027
You should rest now.

00:01:30.111 --> 00:01:32.154
(scoffs)
Life of the party.

00:01:32.238 --> 00:01:34.073
All right, you guys
get some shut-eye.

00:01:34.156 --> 00:01:35.992
-I'll keep watch.
-EDDIE: Don't worry, Buck.

00:01:36.075 --> 00:01:37.284
We got this.

00:01:37.368 --> 00:01:39.537
Nighttime is possum time.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.538
Yeah!

00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:42.415
We own the night, baby.

00:01:42.498 --> 00:01:44.500
(snoring)

00:01:50.381 --> 00:01:52.299
(roaring in distance)

00:01:56.512 --> 00:01:58.139
Good night, Rudy.

00:02:02.018 --> 00:02:04.020
(roaring in distance)

00:02:07.398 --> 00:02:09.608
(chittering)

00:02:10.735 --> 00:02:13.154
Wait, wait.
What about me?

00:02:13.738 --> 00:02:15.281
(sighs)

00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:20.244
(grunting)

00:02:27.543 --> 00:02:29.503
Sleep well, kids.

00:02:29.587 --> 00:02:31.297
We have a busy day tomorrow.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.300
Foraging, hunting.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.928
Missing my friends.

00:02:38.012 --> 00:02:40.556
Probably aren't missing me.

00:02:43.642 --> 00:02:45.352
Huh?

00:02:52.026 --> 00:02:54.528
(sighs affectionately)

00:02:54.612 --> 00:02:57.114
Aw, you're a real softy,
you know that?

00:02:57.198 --> 00:02:59.492
(growls gently)

00:03:03.788 --> 00:03:05.790
(heavy footsteps)

00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:09.627
(low growling)

00:03:15.257 --> 00:03:16.717
(breathing loudly)

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.469
(rustling)

00:03:20.471 --> 00:03:21.847
Manny?

00:03:26.602 --> 00:03:27.895
Crash?

00:03:27.978 --> 00:03:29.355
Eddie?

00:03:33.275 --> 00:03:34.985
Manny?

00:03:43.119 --> 00:03:44.078
(roars)

00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:45.079
(screams)

00:03:45.162 --> 00:03:46.789
(pants)

00:03:53.212 --> 00:03:55.005
What's going on?

00:03:55.089 --> 00:03:56.465
Are you okay?

00:03:56.549 --> 00:03:58.342
Uh... I'm sorry.

00:03:58.425 --> 00:04:01.011
I just wanted
to keep you safe and...

00:04:01.095 --> 00:04:03.430
now you're in
the most dangerous place in the world.

00:04:03.514 --> 00:04:04.515
Hey.

00:04:04.598 --> 00:04:06.016
This isn't your fault.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.685
It's bigger than both of us.

00:04:07.768 --> 00:04:09.687
We have to get Sid.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.357
Yeah, but if I had been
a better friend to him,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.692
we wouldn't be here.

00:04:14.775 --> 00:04:16.318
BUCK:
Better friend?

00:04:16.402 --> 00:04:18.320
Are you plucking my whiskers?

00:04:18.404 --> 00:04:21.407
You risked your life,
your mate, and your baby

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.701
to save your buddy.

00:04:23.784 --> 00:04:27.705
Not the best husband or father,
but a darn good friend.

00:04:33.586 --> 00:04:34.837
(groans)

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.672
-(panting)
-Hey! (groans)

00:04:36.755 --> 00:04:38.382
(squealing and chittering)

00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:40.259
(grunting, growling)

00:04:42.136 --> 00:04:43.512
(tango music playing)

00:04:43.596 --> 00:04:44.763
(growling)

00:04:44.847 --> 00:04:46.849
(grunting)

00:04:54.273 --> 00:04:56.192
(grunting)

00:04:58.986 --> 00:05:00.029
(squeals)

00:05:00.112 --> 00:05:02.114
(grunting)

00:05:05.659 --> 00:05:06.702
(groans)

00:05:06.785 --> 00:05:08.746
(tango continues)

00:05:10.706 --> 00:05:12.917
(choking)

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.710
(screams)

00:05:15.294 --> 00:05:16.629
(sighs)

00:05:16.712 --> 00:05:17.671
(grunts)

00:05:17.755 --> 00:05:19.340
(sighs)

00:05:19.423 --> 00:05:20.424
(squeaky grunt)

00:05:23.385 --> 00:05:24.678
(screams)

00:05:25.763 --> 00:05:28.474
(grunting)

00:05:28.557 --> 00:05:30.434
-(gasps)
-(loud gurgling)

00:05:31.435 --> 00:05:33.520
(whimpers)

00:05:38.692 --> 00:05:41.403
(yelping)

00:05:41.487 --> 00:05:43.447
(belching, hiccupping)

00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:48.452
BUCK:
Everybody stop!

00:05:48.535 --> 00:05:50.204
(sniffing)

00:05:50.287 --> 00:05:51.747
I smell something.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.873
(sniffs)

00:05:52.957 --> 00:05:54.041
(groans)

00:05:56.043 --> 00:05:59.088
Hmm, smells like
a buzzard's butt fell off...

00:05:59.171 --> 00:06:00.547
(sniffing)

00:06:00.631 --> 00:06:03.092
...and then got sprayed on
by a bunch of skunks.

00:06:03.175 --> 00:06:04.301
That's Sid.

00:06:04.385 --> 00:06:05.344
Mammals!

00:06:05.427 --> 00:06:08.305
We have ourselves a crime scene.

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:10.182
A tuft of fur.

00:06:10.266 --> 00:06:12.393
Half-eaten carcass.

00:06:12.476 --> 00:06:13.602
Hunk of...

00:06:13.686 --> 00:06:15.020
Oh, no!

00:06:15.104 --> 00:06:16.021
Broccoli.

00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:17.189
(groans)

00:06:17.273 --> 00:06:18.857
Here's what I think happened.

00:06:18.941 --> 00:06:20.317
Dinosaur attacks Sid.

00:06:20.401 --> 00:06:22.778
Sid fights back
with piece of broccoli,

00:06:22.861 --> 00:06:25.030
leaving dinosaur...

00:06:25.114 --> 00:06:26.615
a vegetable.

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:27.700
Are you nuts?

00:06:27.783 --> 00:06:28.826
Sid's not violent...

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:30.077
or coordinated.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.037
Yeah, and where's the dinosaur?

00:06:32.121 --> 00:06:33.038
All right, all right.

00:06:33.122 --> 00:06:34.290
Good point. (clears throat)

00:06:34.373 --> 00:06:35.666
Theory two.

00:06:35.749 --> 00:06:37.501
Sid's eating broccoli.

00:06:37.584 --> 00:06:38.877
Dinosaur eats Sid.

00:06:38.961 --> 00:06:40.546
Dinosaur steps on broccoli,

00:06:40.629 --> 00:06:41.797
leaving broccoli...

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.674
a vegetable.

00:06:43.757 --> 00:06:45.884
Buck, when exactly
did you lose your mind?

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:46.885
Hmm.

00:06:46.969 --> 00:06:48.053
Three months ago.

00:06:48.137 --> 00:06:50.055
I woke up one morning
married to a pineapple.

00:06:50.723 --> 00:06:52.516
An ugly pineapple.

00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:53.892
(sighs)

00:06:53.976 --> 00:06:54.810
But I loved her.

00:06:54.893 --> 00:06:56.478
DIEGO:
Uh, Buck?

00:06:56.562 --> 00:06:59.898
I think you missed
a little clue over here.

00:06:59.982 --> 00:07:02.651
Well, your friend might be alive,

00:07:02.735 --> 00:07:03.986
but not for long.

00:07:05.154 --> 00:07:06.488
Rudy's closing in.

00:07:06.572 --> 00:07:08.032
(low growling in distance)

00:07:08.115 --> 00:07:09.158
CRASH AND EDDIE:
Whoa.

00:07:09.241 --> 00:07:10.492
BUCK:
You got it.

00:07:10.576 --> 00:07:12.619
The Plates of Woe.

00:07:12.703 --> 00:07:15.247
Or whatever's left of them.

00:07:16.332 --> 00:07:18.250
(gasps, sniffs)

00:07:19.084 --> 00:07:21.503
(whimpers)

00:07:21.587 --> 00:07:22.880
(grunts)

00:07:22.963 --> 00:07:24.340
(gasps)

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.551
(grunts)

00:07:28.385 --> 00:07:29.470
(gasps)

00:07:30.596 --> 00:07:34.475
(straining)

00:07:35.559 --> 00:07:37.394
(groans)

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.482
(gasps)

00:07:42.191 --> 00:07:43.067
(grunts)

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.026
(shouts)

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.237
(gasping)

00:07:50.532 --> 00:07:51.533
SCRATTE:
Huh?

00:07:51.617 --> 00:07:53.869
Hmm?

00:07:56.455 --> 00:07:57.623
(sighing)

00:07:58.332 --> 00:07:59.666
(sighs)

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.587
(romantic music plays)

00:08:04.463 --> 00:08:05.339
(enamored sigh)

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.554
(sniffs)

00:08:12.638 --> 00:08:13.639
(sniffs)

00:08:13.722 --> 00:08:15.599
(both sniffing)

